  "plan": {
    "date": "2026-10-26",
    "baseline_commit": "594134fff063af4496d639d517211822b3996649",
    "problem": "Existing comparison uses only PSNR/SSIM, which is insufficient to assess the expensive LPIPS training path. Add optional reproducible offline LPIPS scoring of the exact aligned evaluation images.",
    "implementation": "Optional --lpips-scorer in compare_quality; a small Brush example loads frozen built-in VGG once and returns per-pair distances. Fail closed on camera/reference/split mismatch or incomplete/invalid scorer results. Keep original output unchanged without the option.",
    "experiment": "Reuse the two successful frozen-LPIPS512/500-step jobs from the previous study; run new500-step512px pipes/office controls with the same frozen engine, identical geometry/seed/flags, LPIPS weight0 instead of0.01. Score matched held-out images at512 using PSNR,SSIM and Brush LPIPS-VGG (lower is better).",
    "limits": "One training run per setting/scene, no statistical quality claim, LPIPS training and scoring share a VGG model so this is not an independent perceptual test. Reused candidate time comes from a previous turn; no controlled speed comparison across turns. No new SfM/end-to-end/peak-memory measurement.",
